WEBVTT

00:03.920 --> 00:07.040
So again you are at the client side and you are data analyst.

00:07.080 --> 00:11.000
You are writing a query where you are defining a CTE called details.

00:11.000 --> 00:12.480
And inside it you have some logic.

00:12.520 --> 00:15.960
And now in the main query you are selecting the data from the orders.

00:15.960 --> 00:21.960
And as well you are joining it with the details with the CTE multiple times using multiple conditions.

00:22.000 --> 00:26.800
Now once you go and execute this query, the database engine can read the query and say aha!

00:26.840 --> 00:30.320
We have here a CTE and it has the main priority.

00:30.320 --> 00:33.400
So that means it's going to go and execute the CTE first.

00:33.440 --> 00:38.760
So and now let's say that in the city you are retrieving data from the table orders and the table orders

00:38.760 --> 00:41.840
of course in that disk storage inside the user data.

00:41.880 --> 00:47.560
And now once the city is completely executed, the database engine can go and place the results in the

00:47.560 --> 00:48.040
cache.

00:48.040 --> 00:50.800
And it's going to name this result as details.

00:50.880 --> 00:52.040
It's like a table name.

00:52.040 --> 00:53.960
So the database engine is done with the CTE.

00:54.000 --> 00:56.400
It's going to go now and grab the main query.

00:56.400 --> 00:58.800
And it's going to start executing it step by step.

00:58.880 --> 01:02.000
So the first step is that to get the data from the orders.

01:02.000 --> 01:06.400
So since the orders exist in the disk storage it's going to go and retrieve it from there.

01:06.440 --> 01:08.460
Now the database engine is going to check the details?

01:08.500 --> 01:10.300
Okay, we have it in the cache.

01:10.300 --> 01:15.220
That means we don't have to search for it in the disk storage, and it can start retrieving the data

01:15.220 --> 01:17.540
from the details with high speed.

01:17.580 --> 01:21.180
And now it's going to go to the second step as well joining the data with the details.

01:21.180 --> 01:25.780
So again the database engine is going to go to the cache and going to see the table details and retrieve

01:25.780 --> 01:27.900
the database maybe in different conditions.

01:27.900 --> 01:30.540
And then to the third time as well we are joining to the details.

01:30.540 --> 01:32.580
And we're going to get the data from the cache.

01:32.580 --> 01:38.620
So as you can see from the main query, we are using the result from the CTE multiple times in different

01:38.620 --> 01:39.300
places.

01:39.300 --> 01:43.580
And the retrieval of all those informations is happening in high speed.

01:43.820 --> 01:50.140
So this is one big benefit of using the CTE is to utilize using the high speed memory of the cache.

01:50.140 --> 01:55.380
So that means retrieving the data from the cache from the details is way faster than retrieving the

01:55.380 --> 01:57.980
data from the disk storage from the orders.

01:58.020 --> 02:03.220
Now, once the main query is completely executed, the result is going to be returned to the database

02:03.220 --> 02:05.740
engine, and then it's going to send it back to the client side.

02:05.740 --> 02:07.940
And we will see the results in the output.

02:07.940 --> 02:08.620
So that's it.

02:08.620 --> 02:09.820
It's amazing right.

02:09.820 --> 02:15.980
This is how the database server execute the amazing technique the CTE behind the scenes.
